WEBVTT

00:00:00.685 --> 00:00:04.720
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> At the end of twenty nineteen, Mark was still looking for Penny.

00:00:05.246 --> 00:00:07.394
Then he found a picture on Facebook.

00:00:08.286 --> 00:00:14.144
<v><b>Mark:</b></v> I wasn’t sure, but I thought it was a photo of Penny, so I messaged the woman,

00:00:14.144 --> 00:00:16.500
and I asked: ‘Is this Penny?’.

00:00:17.086 --> 00:00:21.657
Penny didn’t use Facebook much, so she didn’t see my message immediately.

00:00:22.118 --> 00:00:23.410
But then she replied.

00:00:23.748 --> 00:00:24.844
And it was her!

00:00:25.546 --> 00:00:29.623
<v><b>Penny:</b></v> Mark told me for the first time what had happened at university.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:33.365
I feel very sad and angry about it.

00:00:33.996 --> 00:00:40.199
I think my father didn’t want a Black son-in-law so he told himself he was doing the right thing.

00:00:40.853 --> 00:00:44.070
Now attitudes to race have changed a lot.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.512
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> The couple couldn’t travel to see each other at that time

00:00:47.691 --> 00:00:49.685
because of the COVID-19 pandemic.

00:00:50.325 --> 00:00:56.754
They waited eighteen months, and in June twenty twenty-one, Penny finally flew out to the Bahamas,

00:00:56.882 --> 00:01:00.272
where they met again, aged sixty and sixty-one.

00:01:00.957 --> 00:01:04.417
<v><b>Mark:</b></v> When we saw each other for the first time, I cried.

00:01:04.814 --> 00:01:07.795
I couldn’t believe she was here in my arms.

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:11.795
<v><b>Penny:</b></v> I hadn’t seen him since I was nineteen,

00:01:12.297 --> 00:01:15.229
but it was as if we’d only been apart for a year.

00:01:15.724 --> 00:01:17.458
We hadn’t changed at all.

00:01:18.119 --> 00:01:22.226
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> After three amazing weeks with Mark, Penny came back to England.

00:01:23.005 --> 00:01:26.145
When she returned to the Bahamas in October twenty-one,

00:01:26.472 --> 00:01:28.813
Mark proposed to her when she got off the plane.

00:01:29.537 --> 00:01:32.124
Now Penny is going to live in the Bahamas with him.

00:01:32.863 --> 00:01:35.427
<v><b>Penny:</b></v> I feel like a whole new person.

00:01:36.192 --> 00:01:39.845
I’ve never loved anyone the way I love Mark.

00:01:40.326 --> 00:01:42.610
<v><b>Mark:</b></v> The point we met was not our time.

00:01:43.062 --> 00:01:46.750
Now, we are looking forward to a really great future.